// L'Échiquier de Yohan (Ch2, MAP_GRIS_ECHEC_GYM and MAP_GRIS_ECHEC_GYM_SOURDE):
// contenu-jeu/chapitres/02-gris-echec.md §4. An arena of silence inside a black cube: dark slate
// floors over a black void, black walls whose screens carry Yohan's messages, the hall's glass chess
// king statues, Salle 1's binary tiles (0 left, 1 right), Salle 2's invisible maze (the floor lit
// by the terminal's signal), Salle 3's black and white 8x8 chessboard, and the Chambre Sourde lined
// with grey acoustic foam.
// No ground: the art is the bottom layer. No 1x1 feature sits on 513 or 524 (hygiene: the
// extract has 1x1 layouts of those ids). Features without a prompt are derived art (scratch
// compositing of the generated ones over the floor, see the as-built notes): the lit floor, the
// binary tiles, the wall screen, the statue, the terminal, the warp pad and the foam block on
// their floors.
(
    name: "SilGrisEchecGym",
    primary: "Building",
    style: "Minimalist 16-bit sprite in the Pokemon Ruby/Emerald overworld style (Game Boy Advance). Simple, iconic, low detail: big flat colour areas, 2-3 shades per material, a 1-pixel dark outline, no texture noise, no gradients, no tiny decorations, no anti-aliasing. Dark, silent palette: black, slate grey, with cold cyan light accents.",
    features: [
        (
            name: "sol",
            cells: ["."],
